meta {
  name: Create Campaign Type
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/campaign-types
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "partnerships",
    "label": "Partnerships",
    "description": "Corporate tie-up campaigns",
    "match_keywords": ["partner", "tieup", "corporate"],
    "match_priority": 60,
    "sort_order": 30
  }
}

docs {
  Gated on lms.campaign_types.manage. The tenant comes from the verified
  session, never the body.

  match_keywords are matched case-insensitively ON WORD BOUNDARIES against the
  Meta campaign name by marketing.fn_match_campaign_type() -- so 'hr' does not
  match "Gurugram". Lower match_priority wins when two types both match.

  `name` cannot be changed afterwards and `is_default` is not settable here:
  the name is what weight rows and the Python sync refer to a pool by, and the
  default type is unconditionally visible to everyone.
}
